#: src/canvases/space/sections/heroSection/components/HeroAboutMe.tsx:21
msgid "My name’s Saimands Roy, and I’m a 4th-year Computer Science Engineering student at Central University of Chhattisgarh, Bilaspur. I love building technology that actually does something useful — because a project that only works on localhost is basically a movie trailer with no movie."
msgstr "My name’s Saimands Roy, and I’m a 4th-year Computer Science Engineering student at Central University of Chhattisgarh, Bilaspur. I love building technology that actually does something useful — because a project that only works on localhost is basically a movie trailer with no movie."

#: src/canvases/space/sections/heroSection/components/HeroAboutMe.tsx:44
#~ msgid "My primary focus lies in full-stack development and AI systems from crafting scalable backends with Spring Boot and microservices, to designing AI agents powered by Generative AI and Prompt Engineering. I also love sharpening my problem-solving edge through DSA and competitive programming."
#~ msgstr "My primary focus lies in full-stack development and AI systems from crafting scalable backends with Spring Boot and microservices, to designing AI agents powered by Generative AI and Prompt Engineering. I also love sharpening my problem-solving edge through DSA and competitive programming."

#: src/canvases/space/sections/heroSection/components/HeroAboutMe.tsx:25
msgid "My world revolves around software engineering, backend, and full-stack development. I enjoy turning ideas into scalable systems using Java, Spring Boot, REST APIs, and microservices, while using React and modern frontend technologies to give those systems a face. Lately, I’ve also been exploring Generative AI, AI agents, and Prompt Engineering — teaching machines to think a little smarter, behave a little better, and hopefully stop giving confidently wrong answers."
msgstr "My world revolves around software engineering, backend, and full-stack development. I enjoy turning ideas into scalable systems using Java, Spring Boot, REST APIs, and microservices, while using React and modern frontend technologies to give those systems a face. Lately, I’ve also been exploring Generative AI, AI agents, and Prompt Engineering — teaching machines to think a little smarter, behave a little better, and hopefully stop giving confidently wrong answers."

